# ── Step 226: keychain migration completed and verified; curl in this environment needs a cert FILE, not a keychain identity ──

:step-p12PassphraseKeychainLive a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 226 ;
    schema:name "The uriburner-p12 keychain item is LIVE (migrated from /tmp/uyi with user permission) and verified end-to-end against the real cert.p12 and a real authenticated URIBurner call; separately, this environment's curl cannot consume a Keychain identity for --cert despite the (SecureTransport) version banner — cert loading here is LibreSSL-backed and requires a file path (curl error 58 on both identity-name and SHA-1-hash forms), so the .p12 FILE remains required and Keychain supplies only its passphrase"@en ;
    schema:text "2026-08-18: told the user a SecureTransport banner meant --cert could take a keychain identity name/hash directly, without testing it; the user pushed back, testing then produced curl error 58 for both forms — the claim was wrong and is corrected here rather than repeated." ;
    onto:hasTrigger onto:triggerBehaviorGapIdentified, onto:triggerSkillInvocation ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <howto/keychain-identity-vs-p12-file-curl.ttl>,
        <howto/p12-passphrase-retrieval.ttl#step-keychainPrimary>,
        <preferences.ttl#step-p12PassphraseKeychainFirst> .

# ── Step 238: same Keychain-first pattern applied to a second, independent secret — the local Virtuoso dba password ──

:step-virtuosoLocalDbaKeychain a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 238 ;
    schema:name "Local Virtuoso dba password resolves from macOS Keychain item virtuoso-local-dba FIRST, /tmp/uyi DBA_PWD as fallback — a DISTINCT keychain item from uriburner-p12, never shared"@en ;
    schema:text "2026-08-19: user asked for the p12-passphrase Keychain treatment (Step 224) to be applied to the local Virtuoso dba password too, which was sitting in /tmp/uyi as DBA_PWD=.... Migrated into a new, separately-namespaced item (virtuoso-local-dba) using the identical -T /usr/bin/security / -U pattern, and verified the Keychain value matched the file byte-for-byte before testing. The subsequent isql login test failed (VD CL034 Bad login) — root-caused to the /tmp/uyi value already being stale, not to the migration, since the equality check passed. Only one login attempt was made; no retry loop against a live DBA account, since repeated failures risk lockout. RESOLVED same day: user corrected /tmp/uyi, agent re-synced the Keychain item to the new value and confirmed isql login succeeds using the Keychain-sourced password." ;
    onto:hasTrigger onto:triggerSkillInvocation ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <howto/virtuoso-local-dba-passphrase-retrieval.ttl>,
