        <core.ttl> .

# ── Step 227: name and cross-link the recurring self-grading-checker, false-independence, and fake-edge-test failure classes ──

:step-checkerContextIsolation a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 227 ;
    schema:name "A bundled validator's PASS is a floor not an anchor; two artifacts that look independent may have a real derive-from edge between them; a sequential ordering is only real if the second step needs the first's output or shares a contended external resource"@en ;
    schema:text "2026-08-18: an X/Twitter thread on 'Graph Engineering' (fan-out/reduce/synthesize, checker-context isolation, the fake-edge dependency test, 'anchors' as ground truth a self-grading system cannot fake) prompted a review against this corpus. Two of its three core lessons had already been independently re-learned here across five separate incidents (Steps 169, 173, 174, 186, 187) plus the founding rdf-infographic-gated-workflow.ttl incident, but only as one-off fixes, never named as reusable principles — so named and cross-linked them here." ;
    onto:hasTrigger onto:triggerBehaviorGapIdentified ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <howto/checker-context-isolation.ttl>,
        <howto/generator-script-output-not-a-substitute-for-contract-check.ttl>,
        <howto/rdf-infographic-gated-workflow.ttl>,
        <howto/entity-lookup-disambiguation.ttl> .

# ── Step 228: Step 219's hover-reveal-only edge labels was itself a contract violation — corrected to visible-by-default ──

:step-kgExplorerEdgeLabelsVisibleByDefault a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 228 ;
    schema:name "KG Explorer predicate/edge labels MUST be visible by default (non-zero opacity), not hidden until hover; SKILL.md's Basic Mode bullet lists 'edge/connector labels that are clickable hyperlinks' with no hover qualifier — only the tooltip and line-highlight are explicitly hover behaviors"@en ;
    schema:text "2026-08-19: user flagged a live generated page's opacity:0-by-default predicate labels as a skills-contract and prefs violation, which direct browser/DOM inspection confirmed — see the howto for the full incident and the corrected base-opacity-dimming replacement." ;
